        "displayName": "Protractor Web",
        "readme": "<p>This module demonstrates Serenity/JS web testing capabilities using the legacy Protractor framework as the browser automation tool.</p>\n<h2>Why this module?</h2>\n<p>Protractor has been deprecated, but many Angular teams still have existing test suites built on it. Serenity/JS provides a migration path — the same <code>@serenity-js/web</code> abstractions work across Protractor, Playwright, and WebdriverIO, allowing teams to migrate incrementally.</p>\n<h2>Features demonstrated</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>PageElement interactions via the <code>@serenity-js/web</code> abstraction layer</li>\n<li>BrowseTheWebWithProtractor ability implementation</li>\n<li>Same portable web specs as Playwright and WebdriverIO</li>\n<li>Angular-specific waiting and synchronisation via Protractor</li>\n</ul>\n"
